course: dictionary
lesson: 2454
title: Dangerously
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dangerously is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or how something is. It means in a way that could cause harm or injury. Spot the root word danger inside it, and the -ly ending shows it describes the action or state.
explain: «A dog must never be left in a parked car, because it gets dangerously hot in minutes.» Dangerously hot does not just mean a bit hot. It means hot enough to hurt. Test it: swap in "very hot" and the warning feels weaker, so dangerously carries the risk.
explain: Dangerously can also go with close or near, as in «dangerously close». This means so close that something bad could easily happen, like standing right at the edge of a cliff.
fact: Dangerously means in a way that could cause harm or injury.
fact: Dangerously is an adverb: it tells you how something is done or how bad something is.
fact: «Dangerously close» or «dangerously near» means so close that something bad could easily happen.
fact: «Dangerously hot», «dangerously cold» and «dangerously ill» all show a level that could cause real harm.
fact: A quick check: swap in "in a risky way" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Shivering hard and being very sleepy can be signs a person is getting dangerously cold.» What does dangerously mean here? | In a bright and happy way | Only a little bit | *In a way that could cause harm | In a very slow and gentle way
exercise: «Standing dangerously close to the edge of the cliff.» What does dangerously close mean? | Close, in the middle of a field | *So close that something bad could easily happen | Close to the edge, but very safe | Far away from the edge
exercise: «The car got dangerously hot inside.» Copy the word that tells how hot the car got. | got | car | sun | *dangerously
test: Mia says dangerously means "very nicely". What does it really mean? | Bravely and happily | In a neat and careful way | Very quietly | *In a way that could cause harm or injury
test: «Some people are dangerously allergic to stings.» Which phrase means nearly the same as dangerously here? | Quietly | Slightly | Mildly | *Seriously, and at risk of harm
exam: Pick the sentence where dangerously is used correctly: | *The ice looked dangerously thin, so no one walked on it. | My new shoes are dangerously blue. | The cat purred dangerously in the sun. | She sang dangerously beautifully.
